  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "the loss of supply air to the Main Air Ejector Steam Pressure Control valve was the result of the Instrument Air Pressure Control Valve failing to provide adequate output pressure to maintain the valve in the open position. A failure analysis concluded the supply air flow-path of the Instrument Air Pressure Control Valve was obstructed due to poor manufacturing quality resulting in lowered output pressure.",
